  "notes": "West leads the ♥Q against 3NT. There are 8 top tricks (2 spades, 2 hearts, 3 diamonds, and the ♣A). West's heart lead is won by South.\n\nPlaying on clubs is too dangerous as an unfavourable break in either clubs or hearts will defeat the contract. South should look towards spades for trick 9.\n\nThe spade combination looks like a standard finessing position. It looks like South should cash a top spade in dummy, cross in diamonds, and finesse the ♠J . This plan will work whenever West has the ♠Q and when East has the ♠Q with spades breaking 3-3.\n\nThis plan can be improved so that the contract can be made if East has a doubleton ♠Q. After cashing a top spade from dummy, the other top honour should be cashed. If the ♠Q drops, South will succeed immediately.\n\nIf, after playing the other top honour, the ♠Q does not appear, South can cross in diamonds and lead towards the ♠J. South still will succeed if West has the ♠Q or if spades are 3-3. The ♣A will act as an entry to the hoped for ninth trick in spades.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
